{
    "word": "gristle",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b66794b0-5581-3c95-9279-27048a6d085e",
                "word": "gristle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e86f2393-d194-443c-a398-82350af78d4b",
                        "entry_id": "b66794b0-5581-3c95-9279-27048a6d085e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gristles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dadaaf85-0bd5-312d-9658-79e17f10c3dd",
                        "entry_id": "b66794b0-5581-3c95-9279-27048a6d085e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Cartilage; now especially: cartilage present, as a tough substance, in meat."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "50fd2b70-d6b7-4be2-b381-05a2e49814af",
                                "sense_id": "dadaaf85-0bd5-312d-9658-79e17f10c3dd",
                                "text": "When you're chewing on life's gristle\nDon't grumble, give a whistle\nAnd this'll help things turn out for the best[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f014158-a1f7-411e-9508-f8f11233b354",
                                "sense_id": "dadaaf85-0bd5-312d-9658-79e17f10c3dd",
                                "text": "But she was tired of cell culture, tired of meticulously cutting away dead tissue like gristle from a steak […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5db6a09c-d912-342b-b9c8-90e662758133",
                        "entry_id": "b66794b0-5581-3c95-9279-27048a6d085e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bone not yet hardened by age and hard work."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e1bf453-4aba-4164-afc4-cd1af03fe9c9",
                                "sense_id": "5db6a09c-d912-342b-b9c8-90e662758133",
                                "text": "And it is a hard and cruel thing thus in early youth to taste beforehand the pangs which should be reserved for the stout time of manhood, when the gristle has become bone, and we stand up and fight out our lives, as a thing tried before and foreseen; for then we are veterans used to sieges and battles, and not green recruits, recoiling at the first shock of the encounter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "059f0a17-fa06-4a01-b5e4-c2ae83490460",
                                "sense_id": "5db6a09c-d912-342b-b9c8-90e662758133",
                                "text": "Look at Adam through the rest of the day, as he stands on the scaffolding with the two-feet ruler in his hand, whistling low while he considers how a difficulty about a floor-joist or a window-frame is to be overcome; or as he pushes one of the younger workmen aside and takes his place in upheaving a weight of timber, saying, \"Let alone, lad! Thee'st got too much gristle i' thy bones yet\"; or as he fixes his keen black eyes on the motions of a workman on the other side of the room and warns him that his distances are not right."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4fba6dad-a93c-4068-897c-ad8b5a2e7811",
                                "sense_id": "5db6a09c-d912-342b-b9c8-90e662758133",
                                "text": "1885, Ada Sarah Ballin, The Science of Dress in Theory and Practice,\nIt. must be borne in mind that the bones of a young infant are little more than gristle, and are liable to bend, and so become deformed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdaf7b11-6721-434f-bcff-0002cad21f23",
                                "sense_id": "5db6a09c-d912-342b-b9c8-90e662758133",
                                "text": "\"The young 'un will make his way,\" said Belcher, who had come across to us. \"He's more a sparrer than a fighter just at present, but when his gristle sets he'll take on anything on the list."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "58b44570-4509-4738-9f07-c25b4fdf456a",
                        "source_entry_id": "b66794b0-5581-3c95-9279-27048a6d085e",
                        "source_sense_description": "cartilage",
                        "target_lang_word": "kraakbeen",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kraakbeen",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d618b8f-15d7-3aef-9308-d31a4b524431",
                                        "entry_id": "f568cb1b-fc93-3806-8a3b-e81bf3f67306",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "een speciale vorm van bindweefsel met een elastisch karakter als gevolg van eigenschappen van de extracellulaire matrix"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8b613ab-43c0-473b-b4e2-49df0fb60a46",
                                                "sense_id": "3d618b8f-15d7-3aef-9308-d31a4b524431",
                                                "text": "Kraakbeen bestaat voornamelijk uit collageenvezels in een matrix van chondroitinesulfaat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5ac3da30-22a9-42a0-ba6e-205837146f5c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b66794b0-5581-3c95-9279-27048a6d085e",
                        "source_sense_description": "cartilage",
                        "target_lang_word": "cartilage",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cartilage",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "316b4fc9-13c0-39d3-914b-190387d44c27",
                                        "entry_id": "5b870e99-0d20-3774-b2e6-9cac525ccd46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Partie blanche, dure, lisse, élastique, qui se trouve surtout aux extrémités des os, et qui forme le squelette entier de certains poissons."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11507f3c-28fd-4665-b70f-f22406b18076",
                                                "sense_id": "316b4fc9-13c0-39d3-914b-190387d44c27",
                                                "text": "L’enclouure sera grave, si le pus, après avoir long-temps séjourné dans le pied, a carié l'os, ou si, après avoir fusé dessous la chair de la couronne, il a gâté, ou le tendon extenseur, ou le cartilage latéral, ou l'articulation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f59a165-3d87-486a-b1ad-7c4475636ebf",
                                                "sense_id": "316b4fc9-13c0-39d3-914b-190387d44c27",
                                                "text": "Après avoir traîné vingt ans ses os et ses cartilages dans les garnisons ou sur les champs de bataille, il avait obtenu d’être incorporé dans un escadron de gendarmerie du Loiret, où sa minutieuse rigidité fut inégalable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6b77a2c-24b2-4fe1-81f2-ff229e46ddbf",
                                                "sense_id": "316b4fc9-13c0-39d3-914b-190387d44c27",
                                                "text": "Les lésions du cartilage ont été longtemps négligées bien que parfaitement décrites."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9655f4b9-cb63-4e7f-b450-82e05395086a",
